{"name":"Atlas Red","hex":"#82193a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"atlas","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bound collection of maps often including tables, illustrations or other text.","A bound collection of tables, illustrations, etc. on any given subject."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich satin fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atlas"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Atlas","blocks":[{"text":"An atlas is a collection of maps; it is typically a bundle of maps of Earth or of a continent or region of Earth. Advances in astronomy have also resulted in atlases of the celestial sphere or of other planets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Mercator_-_Atlas_-_1595.png/330px-Mercator_-_Atlas_-_1595.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlas","wikidata":"Q162827"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/89v_90r_%D9%86%D8%B2%D9%87%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A7%D9%82_Arabe_2221_BNF.jpg/500px-89v_90r_%D9%86%D8%B2%D9%87%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A7%D9%82_Arabe_2221_BNF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/89v_90r_%D9%86%D8%B2%D9%87%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A7%D9%82_Arabe_2221_BNF.jpg/1280px-89v_90r_%D9%86%D8%B2%D9%87%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A7%D9%82_Arabe_2221_BNF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/89v_90r_%D9%86%D8%B2%D9%87%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A7%D9%82_Arabe_2221_BNF.jpg/500px-89v_90r_%D9%86%D8%B2%D9%87%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A7%D9%82_Arabe_2221_BNF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Maghreb (south-up) in Muhammad al-Idrisi's Nuzhat al-Mushtāq (نزهة المشتاق في اختراق الآفاق), also known as the Tabula Rogeriana (12th century).[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A89v_90r_%D9%86%D8%B2%D9%87%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A7%D9%82_Arabe_2221_BNF.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Theatrum_Orbis_Terrarum%2C_by_Abraham_Ortelius%2C_World%2C_1572.jpg/500px-Theatrum_Orbis_Terrarum%2C_by_Abraham_Ortelius%2C_World%2C_1572.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Theatrum_Orbis_Terrarum%2C_by_Abraham_Ortelius%2C_World%2C_1572.jpg/12